[[Open This|2. Initial install]]

---

Boot from your media. The install media will log in automatically as root and display an informational banner:

```yml
 -- Welcome to Oxide Helios! -------------------------------------------------

    This bootable ISO allows you to install Helios on a traditional
    install-to-disk system; e.g., a desktop PC or a BIOS/EFI-boot
    server.

    To install, use "diskinfo" to locate the disk you wish to install
    to, and then use "install-helios" to format it and install the
    operating system.

    More information is available in the "Installing on a physical
    machine using the ISO" section of the README at:

        https://github.com/oxidecomputer/helios-engvm

 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
```

From this shell:

Run diskinfo to find your disk; <span style="font-family: 'Beleren', sans-serif; color: #00d892;">you may need to run it a few times if the disk devices have not yet finished attaching and you don't see the disks you expect.</span> For example:

```
# diskinfo
TYPE  DISK                    VID      PID              SIZE          RMV SSD
NVME  c1t0025385C9150D623d0   Samsung  SSD 970 EVO 1TB   931.51 GiB   no  yes
NVME  c2t0014EE83021EAE80d0   NVMe     WUS4BB019D4M9E4  1788.50 GiB   no  yes
```
wolfoxide

```yml
michael@wolfoxide:~$ su
Password:
# diskinfo
TYPE    DISK                    VID      PID              SIZE          RMV SSD
SCSI    c1t1d1                  ATA      ST2000NM0033-9ZM 1863.02 GiB   no  no
SCSI    c1t0d1                  ATA      ST2000NM0033-9ZM 1863.02 GiB   no  no
SCSI    c1t2d1                  ATA      ST2000NM0033-9ZM 1863.02 GiB   no  no
```

Choose a hostname.

Run the installer, providing the hostname you've chosen and the disk onto which you wish to install; e.g.,

```
# install-helios myhostname c1t0025385C9150D623d0
...
ok to reboot now
```

* Once you get the "ok to reboot now" prompt, you should be able to remove the media and boot from your installed disk.
* After reboot, log in with root and no password.